msgid "tale.hare"
msgstr "The Pomor hare is a shy beast: it tangles its tracks and sits breathless under a tussock in the fog. They say whoever sees the first hare in spring has an easy road. (TODO: author's tale)"

msgid "tale.fox"
msgstr "The fox walks the edge of the fog and listens for the axe. The old folk said a fox by the house means guests are coming. (TODO: author's tale)"

msgid "tale.seal"
msgstr "The seal hauls out on the rocks and watches the boat for a long, long time. Pomors never touched seals on their own skerries — bad luck. Here you can only watch her. (TODO: author's tale)"

msgid "tale.gull"
msgstr "The gull is a thief: where there's a fish rack, there's a gull. But gulls over the water mean land is near. (TODO: author's tale)"

msgid "tale.reindeer"
msgstr "The wild reindeer comes down to the water at sunset and leaves if you speak loudly. (TODO: author's tale)"

msgid "tale.wolf"
msgstr "At night the wolf circles the fire but never steps inside. Walk with a torch and he won't touch you. (TODO: author's tale)"

msgid "tale.bear"
msgstr "The master of the woods first rears up and roars — that's his warning. Walk away and he won't follow. (TODO: author's tale)"

msgid "tale.polar_bear"
msgstr "The oshkuy, the white bear, walks the ice of the Frozen Sea and remembers everyone who entered his grounds. (TODO: author's tale)"

msgid "tale.mglyak"
msgstr "The mistling is a tuft of fog with eyes. Its touch puts out fire, and it backs away from fire. (TODO: author's tale)"

msgid "tale.kikimora"
msgstr "The bog kikimora sits in the sedge and throws mud at travellers to trip them. (TODO: author's tale)"

msgid "tale.morok"
msgstr "The glamour lights a false fire in the fog that looks like a beacon and leads boats onto rocks. Trust the compass, not the light. (TODO: author's tale)"

msgid "tale.fog_wolf"
msgstr "Fog wolves hunt in a pack and in silence. You only hear the moss crunch. (TODO: author's tale)"

msgid "tale.ice_mglyak"
msgstr "The frost mistling breathes cold: after its breath your hands can't hold the spear. (TODO: author's tale)"

msgid "tale.domovoy"
msgstr "The domovoy lives behind the stove when the house is warm and at peace. Leave him kalitki and your chests stay tidy and the house cosy. (TODO: author's tale)"

msgid "tale.bannik"
msgstr "The bannik lives in the bathhouse. The third steam is his: don't steam after midnight, don't anger the master. (TODO: author's tale)"

msgid "tale.leshy"
msgstr "The leshy leads you round the woods in the fog. Leave cloudberries on a stump and his green wisp leads you to the path. (TODO: author's tale)"

msgid "tale.vodyanoy"
msgstr "The vodyanoy sits by the water, his beard in weed. Give him the first fish of the day and the bites last till evening. (TODO: author's tale)"

msgid "tale.sirin"
msgstr "At dawn Sirin, the bird-maiden, sings on the rocks. Whoever hears her song never forgets it — and the sea takes up her tune. (TODO: author's tale)"

msgid "tale.ryba_kit"
msgstr "The Miracle Whale surfaces on calm nights with a tiny chapel on its back. Whoever moors there rests until dawn. (TODO: author's tale)"

msgid "tale.chud"
msgstr "The White-Eyed Chud went under the earth when strangers came. Only their mines and stone circles remain. (TODO: author's tale)"

msgid "tale.likho"
msgstr "One-Eyed Likho sleeps in a cave on the Summer Shore. It has one eye — you can slip past on the side without one. (TODO: author's tale)"

msgid "tale.karachun"
msgstr "Karachun, the frost spirit, walks the Frozen Sea by night and puts out lanterns. He fears fire. (TODO: author's tale)"

msgid "tale.siverko"
msgstr "Siverko is the north wind. He blows you off the ledges and lashes you with ice needles. (TODO: author's tale)"

msgid "tale.bolotnitsa"
msgstr "The Bog Maiden drags you into the mire and calls the kikimoras. Fire burns her. (TODO: author's tale)"

msgid "tale.hozyain_guby"
msgstr "The Master of the Bay rises from the sea by the shore rocks and drives waves onto the land. (TODO: author's tale)"

msgid "tale.mga"
msgstr "The Mga is the heart of the fog. It swallows lights and breaks into mistlings. It weakens while every lantern around burns. (TODO: author's tale)"

msgid "tale.chud.1"
msgstr "A sign is cut into the stone: a circle and three lines. Under it, a handful of mica. (TODO: author's tale)"

msgid "tale.chud.2"
msgstr "They say the Chud went into these mines singing, and the song can be heard on a quiet night. (TODO: author's tale)"

msgid "tale.chud.3"
msgstr "Old iron in the earth never rusts — the Chud way. (TODO: author's tale)"

msgid "tale.chud.4"
msgstr "Whoever takes a stone from the circle loses the way home. The stones stay put. (TODO: author's tale)"

msgid "tale.chud.5"
msgstr "The air in the mines is warm, as if someone breathes under the earth. (TODO: author's tale)"

msgid "tale.chud.6"
msgstr "The Chud were never enemies: they left rather than fight. They left us their signs. (TODO: author's tale)"

